  "rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and, in the text field, the passage of about 250 words that comes immediately AFTER the current text in the same story.",
  "text": "When Elara opened her eyes, the lighthouse was gone. She stood on a shore of black sand, grains shifting like living things beneath her feet, each one humming with a faint, residual energy. The sky above was not the gray expanse of the storm, but a deep, velvety indigo, dotted with stars that pulsed in rhythm with her own heartbeat. The air tasted of salt and ozone, thick with the scent of ancient rain. She looked down at her hands; they were translucent, shimmering with the same liquid light that had consumed her moments ago. She was no longer entirely human, nor entirely sea, but something in between, a hybrid of flesh and current. A figure emerged from the mist ahead, tall and slender, composed of swirling water and shadow. It was the Keeper, the one who had tended the beacon for centuries, though his form was now fluid, lacking the rigid structure of bone and muscle. He did not speak, but a wave of understanding washed over Elara. She was not lost; she was found. The ocean had been waiting for her, for a bridge between the world of men and the realm of the deep. She took a step forward, the black sand parting gently to receive her, and felt the vast, singing dark embrace her once more, no longer as a void, but as a home."
