  "text": "Kael didn’t move. The air between them felt thick, charged with the static of unspoken accusations and the weight of a shared past that had bled them both dry. He looked at the device, then back at her, searching for the lie in her eyes. He found none, only the desperate, hollow look of someone who had run out of options. \"You know I can’t trust you,\" he said, his voice rough, scraping against the silence. \"Not after what you did. Not after you left me to rot in that cell while you vanished into the shadows.\" Elara flinched, but she didn’t look away. \"I know,\" she whispered. \"And I’m sorry. But apologies don’t stop bullets, Kael. And they don’t stop Vane from tearing this city apart to find that thing in my hand.\" A distant shout echoed from the alleyway behind them, sharp and commanding, followed by the crunch of boots on wet pavement. The sound was closer now, urgent and predatory. Kael’s hand finally left his hip, not to draw his weapon, but to grip Elara’s shoulder. The contact was electric, shocking them both. \"Then we move,\" he said, his decision final. \"But we do it my way. No more secrets. No more running alone. If you try to betray me again, I won’t hesitate.\" Elara nodded, her eyes hardening. She tucked the device into her jacket, the hum fading as it went dormant. \"Deal,\" she said. Together, they slipped into the shadows, moving with a synchronized grace born of necessity, leaving the safety of the abandoned warehouse behind and stepping into the dark, uncertain night where the real hunt was just beginning."
